  "slug": "espinacas-con-garbanzos-spinach-with-garbanzo-beans",
  "name": "Espinacas con Garbanzos (Spinach with Garbanzo Beans)",
  "recipe_type": "appetizer",
  "brief_description": "This recipe can be eaten as a side dish or as a light meal. It's great with a grilled pork chop and some crusty bread. Its origins date back to North African cultures and is one of the very popular choices of tapas in Seville's bars.",
  "cuisine": "Spanish",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Heat the olive oil in a skillet over medium-low heat. Cook the garlic and onion in the oil until translucent, about 5 minutes. Stir in the spinach, garbanzo beans, cumin, and salt. Use your stirring spoon to lightly mash the beans as the mixture cooks. Allow to cook until thoroughly heated."
    }
  ],
